I discovered the option [`--source-policy-file`](https://github.com/podman-container-tools/buildah/blob/71606d426148bb5b543fe930f68400b8514e37cd/docs/buildah-build.1.md?plain=1#L1088-L1147)
```
$ podman build --help | grep source-policy-file
      --source-policy-file pathname                  pathname of source policy file for controlling source references during build
```

Demo:

1. Create file `/tmp/policy.json` containing
   ```json
   {
     "rules": [
       {
         "action": "DENY",
         "selector": {
           "identifier": "docker-image://docker-archive:*",
           "matchType": "WILDCARD"
         }
       },
       {
         "action": "DENY",
         "selector": {
           "identifier": "docker-image://oci-archive:*",
           "matchType": "WILDCARD"
         }
       },
       {
         "action": "DENY",
         "selector": {
           "identifier": "docker-image://oci:*",
           "matchType": "WILDCARD"
         }
       }
     ]
   }
   ```
2. Create directory
   ```
   mkdir ctr
   ```
3. Change directory
   ```
   cd ctr
   ```
4. Create file `foobar` with `skopeo`
   ```
   skopeo copy -q docker://docker.io/library/alpine:3.20.9 docker-archive:./foobar:docker.io/library/fedora:43
   ```
5. Create file `Containerfile` containing
   ```
   FROM docker-archive:./foobar
   ```
6. Build container image
   ```
   podman build --source-policy-file /tmp/policy.json .
   ```
   The command fails with the error message
   ```
   Error: source "docker-archive:./foobar" denied by source policy: matched rule 0 (selector: "docker-image://docker-archive:*")
   ```




__side note:__  the following policy does not work:

```json
{
  "rules": [
    {
      "action": "DENY",
      "selector": {
        "identifier": "docker-archive:*",
        "matchType": "WILDCARD"
      }
    },
    {
      "action": "DENY",
      "selector": {
        "identifier": "oci-archive:*",
        "matchType": "WILDCARD"
      }
    },
    {
      "action": "DENY",
      "selector": {
        "identifier": "oci:*",
        "matchType": "WILDCARD"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```
(I would have expected it to work to specify `docker-archive:*` instead of `docker-image://docker-archive:*`)
